  "interpretation": [
    "The host-only preload optimization worked in the narrow sense: median unsampled full-chunk transfer time falls from 10,780 to 9,196 us and delivered throughput rises about 10.6%. This does not satisfy the playback objective.",
    "The measured 1.578 MB/s supply is still only about 67.7% of the clip average requirement. At this mean, the largest meadow picture needs about 161 ms of input against 33.37 ms per nominal frame, consistent with continued visible slow passages.",
    "Longest retained presentation holds remain 166.833 ms. Thus the user report of everything looking the same is compatible with a modest improvement in whole-clip duration.",
    "Extended ACK-low polling appears in 7 of 33 sampled chunks, versus 1 before; the new maximum is 76 reads. Faster delivery encountering downstream flow control more often is a plausible explanation, not a measured allocation of FIFO-wait duration. Preserve flow control.",
    "The first three retained delayed deadlines still find decoder input ready but empty. Nonzero writer-capacity blocked cycles are 22, 0 and 255 and must not be described as zero.",
    "decoder_stall_cycles increases from 214,276,305 to 515,458,144, but its RTL increments only when fifo_pending and not decoder_ready; it is not an unconditional decode-time measure. Greater input availability changes which busy cycles count, so this increase does not itself prove a decoder regression."
  ],
  "measurement_limits": [
    "Delivery uses matched completed-chunk endpoints: subtract first submitted bytes as well as first timestamp; it is not a count-divided-by-total-time startup average.",
    "One run per changed condition is not a controlled statistical effect-size estimate. No identical repeat is requested.",
    "ACK counters cover only every 64th successful data chunk, exclude command-byte handshakes and report read counts rather than durations. More-than-one-read wait-word counts are mostly the ordinary two-read handshake.",
    "Largest-gap picture identifiers are eight bits and ambiguous after 256 pictures. Do not place raw codes 95, 98 or 15 at unique absolute source positions.",
    "deadline_gap_count counts delayed eventual presentation intervals, not every missed nominal frame slot.",
    "Poll durations measure main-loop blocking exposure, not direct UI response. The user reports everything the same but does not separately assess current menu response.",
    "Bob/Weave mode is not encoded here. The old spikes issue refers to historical progressive bring-up, not this comparison.",
    "The qualified 8 Mbps regression, unsupported interlaced features, audio/PTS, partial-transfer cancellation and old live-raster assertion drift remain outstanding."
  ],
  "next_boundary": "Host-only removal of one register write per word is insufficient. Propose a coordinated core-specific host/FPGA transport mode that amortizes acknowledgement across bounded bursts backed by conservatively reported FIFO capacity, with explicit ordering/drain guarantees, reset/fallback behavior and overflow/byte-count verification. Read-only design work can proceed; implementation requires approval for this material protocol change and full RTL/Quartus/timing qualification. Do not simply drop existing ACK waits, enlarge the clean-video queue, change startup/sync or promise transport alone removes every decoder limit. Preserve the current qualified host as the comparison/restore point; no binary is changed in this evidence cycle.",
