    "identified_prior_recommendation": "Entries579/580 proposed spi_block_write -> fpga_spi_fast_block_write; entry581 corrected the unsafe assumption that it could replace acknowledged writes without FIFO flow control.",
    "current_architecture": "MediaPlayer_Helper writes annotated bytes to stdout; Main reads the pipe and owns FPGA transfers. The helper does not currently talk directly to FPGA registers.",
    "current_bulk_vs_fast": "be8502b removes one redundant GPO write per data word but retains both ACK phases. The pinned fast block loop has two GPO writes per word plus one final low write and no per-word ACK reads, through the same general-purpose-register link.",
    "distinct_bridge_option": "Pinned Main also exposes fpga_core_write/read for the lightweight HPS-to-FPGA address window. A dedicated memory-mapped receiver or shared-memory/DMA design would be a separate FPGA transport implementation, not an existing MediaPlayer helper option.",
    "speed_claim": "No measured 10 MB/s result for this MediaPlayer target was found in the reviewed evidence. Higher throughput from fewer synchronous round trips is plausible, but the number must be measured, and receiver limits remain.",
